    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "W is external mutable reality, stably bound by SubjectBinding b_W. A bounded observation q_n, separately identified operation op_n, owner-issued grant g_n, invocation inv_n and EffectSubject s_n support readiness before dispatch; later observation and disposition support a separate TransitionSubject judgment. Functor kind, traversal, operation, executor, actor, grant and invocation remain different coordinates.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1094,
          "quote": "op_n is a separately identified domain operation.\ng_n is the exact owner-issued grant for op_n over b_W.\ninv_n = EffectInvocation(o_n, op_n, executor_n, actor_n, g_n, territory_n, inputs_n)\ns_n = EffectSubject(o_n, b_W, q_n, inv_n, op_n, g_n, territory_n, invalidation_n)\nj_ready = judge_effect_readiness(s_n)",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FMutable-Subject%20Effect%20Relation",
