    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "An EventFrontier binds profile basis, scope, precedence law, sorted event identities and event content digests. For each (basis, scope, precedence law) there is one empty frontier. A Projection binds its exact frontier, projection rule, selected relation identities, boundary identities and residual identities.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 1228,
          "quote": "For profile basis `b`, scope `s`, and precedence law `p`, there is one empty\nfrontier `F_0(b,s,p)`. Admitting event `e_k_plus_1` constructs a successor whose\nmember set is exactly `members(F_k) union {e_k_plus_1}`. Frontier identity binds\nthe profile basis, scope, precedence law, sorted event identities, and event\ncontent digests. Projection identity binds the exact frontier, projection\nrule, selected relation ids, boundary ids, and residual ids.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FEvent%20Frontier%20And%20Projection",
