    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "UX_METHOD.md is the UX realization method document. Its heading and profile-binding marker introduce the document rather than an executed adoption.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 3,
          "quote": "# UX Method\n\n<!-- STDO3_PROFILE_BINDING_START -->",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method",
          "start_line": 1
        }
      ],
      "key": "ux_method",
      "label": "UX Method"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Within the method's covered UX surface."],
      "definition": "Elm Architecture is the constitutional UX process model: runtime-owned typed State; Msg algebra for every user/system action; pure Update : (Msg, State) → (State, Cmd); deterministic pure View : State → ViewTree; typed Cmd/Sub descriptions interpreted by the runtime at the effect membrane. The runtime owns the loop from State through View, Msg, Update and Cmd interpretation back to State.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 157,
          "quote": "- **State** — typed state shape held by the runtime, not by the view\n- **Msg** — typed message algebra naming every action a user or system can emit\n- **Update** — pure reducer of signature `(Msg, State) → (State, Cmd)`; describes side effects as `Cmd` values, does not perform them\n- **View** — pure function of signature `State → ViewTree`; given the same state, produces the same output\n- **Cmd / Sub** — typed descriptions of side effects to schedule and external sources to subscribe to; interpreted by the runtime at the effect membrane\n\nThe runtime owns the loop:\n\n`current State → render View → user emits Msg → Update produces new State and Cmds → runtime interprets Cmds → repeat`",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method%2F4.%20Process%20Model%20%E2%80%94%20Elm%20Architecture",
          "start_line": 149
        }
      ],
      "key": "elm_architecture",
      "label": "Elm Architecture"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The named upstream method roles are: SPEC—constitutional process, authority flow, lawful re-entry, repricing and migration; DESIGN_MODULE—deterministic module realization, including immutability, totality, effect-edge discipline, no-semantic-center and coupling; ODD—graph-native constructive carrier, execution shape and traversal law; TICKET—ticket/sprint lifecycle. These are referenced roles, not reconstructed external methods.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 93,
          "quote": "`UX_METHOD.md` does not duplicate `DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md`. Where the parent method already governs (immutability, totality, effect-edge discipline, no-semantic-center, coupling), `UX_METHOD.md` cites and extends it. Where UX has concerns the parent does not address (render lifecycle, browser events, layout, accessibility), `UX_METHOD.md` is authoritative.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method%2F2.%20Method%20Role",
          "start_line": 93
        },
        {
          "end_line": 599,
          "quote": "- `SPEC_METHOD.md` governs constitutional process, authority flow, repricing, and migration law.\n- `ODD_METHOD.md` governs graph-native constructive carrier law. UX surfaces are projection / query surfaces under §10 of that method.\n- `DESIGN_MODULE_METHOD.md` governs deterministic realization discipline at the module level. `UX_METHOD.md` refines it for UX modules.\n- `TICKET_METHOD.md` governs ticket and sprint lifecycle. UX work may use sprint compliance escrow under §13B when the sprint boundary makes deferred proof visible, bounded, and payable.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method%2F16.%20Relationship%20To%20Other%20Method%20Surfaces",
          "start_line": 596
        }
      ],
      "key": "referenced_method_roles",
      "label": "Referenced constitutional and realization methods"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "The declared effect membrane interprets reducer-produced Cmd values and returns typed outcome Msg values to the reducer. It is an effect interpreter, not a second business-continuation controller.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 225,
          "quote": "The membrane interprets `Cmd` values produced by the reducer and translates side-effect outcomes back into `Msg` values delivered to the reducer.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method%2F6.%20Effect%20Membrane%20Rule",
          "start_line": 225
        }
      ],
      "key": "ux_effect_membrane",
      "label": "UX effect membrane"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "Msg-replay proof is an executable assessment of an exact product-meaningful interaction family, with initial State, ordered Msg log, expected final State, ordered Cmd values, typed effect-return Msg cases and injected deterministic time, randomness, generated identities and external payloads.",
      "exceptions": ["A pure projection-only surface may use the declared no-effect proof."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 312,
          "quote": "- an initial `State` fixture\n- an ordered `Msg` log\n- the expected final `State`\n- the expected ordered `Cmd` values\n- the typed outcome `Msg` values returned by interpreted `Cmd`s, including\n  unresolved effects wherever admitted by the interaction contract\n- injected deterministic values for time, randomness, generated ids, and\n  external payloads",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/UX_METHOD.md#UX%20Method%2F8.%20UX%20Twin%20Of%20ODD%20%C2%A711.5A%20%E2%80%94%20View%20Does%20Not%20Own%20Continuation%2F8A.%20Msg-Replay%20Proof%20Requirement",
          "start_line": 305
