      "key": "world_model_method",
      "label": "World Model Method"
    },
    {
      "conditions": [],
      "definition": "A world model is a governed, inspectable, versioned, machine-reasonable semantic layer over authoritative source systems. It is descriptive before generative; it traces sources, records accepted claims in ledgers and publishes bounded cuts for reasoning. Records require function, provenance and treatment context; catalogs and schemas are explanatory projections. Institutional systems enact bounded function through code, events, records, APIs, schedules, configurations, documents and downstream obligations.",
      "exceptions": [],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 89,
          "quote": "- source systems enact domain function and remain sovereign for operational\n  truth\n- domains are defined by bounded function and authority\n- records are intelligible only through function, provenance, and treatment\n  context\n- mappings are semantic treatments over governed meaning\n- catalogs and schemas are explanatory projections over deeper semantic\n  structure\n- the world model traces authoritative source surfaces, records accepted\n  semantic claims in ledgers, and publishes bounded semantic cuts\n- the published semantic layer gives probabilistic systems a governed substrate\n  for reasoning and correspondence",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FPosition",
          "start_line": 78
        },
        {
          "end_line": 262,
          "quote": "A world model is a governed semantic layer built over existing source systems.\n\nIt is descriptive before it is generative.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FWhat%20A%20World%20Model%20Is",
          "start_line": 260
        }
      ],
      "key": "world_model",
      "label": "World model"
    },
    {
      "conditions": ["Imported under the selected complete STDO basis with the SPEC owner retained."],
      "definition": "The exact imported recursive-product-taxonomy concepts are source-project, product, install and artifact at urn:stdo:concept:recursive-product-taxonomy:<name>. Source Project means the mutable workspace building the next release cut; Product means a released immutable thing; Install means a stamped workspace instance; Artifact means published output. PRODUCT.md is the mutable Source Project's product-definition surface, not its released Product artifact.",
      "exceptions": ["No other same-spelled concept is imported."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 154,
          "quote": "- `Product` retains the released immutable-thing meaning; a builder or runtime\n  may be one such Product;\n- `Install` retains the stamped-workspace-instance meaning;\n- `Source Project` retains the mutable-workspace-building-the-next-release-cut\n  meaning;\n- `Artifact` retains the published-output meaning; and\n- `PRODUCT.md` remains the product-definition surface of a mutable Source\n  Project, not the released Product artifact itself.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FMethod%20Role",
