      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 765,
          "quote": "Every admitted constraint evaluation returns the shared\n[result record](FOUNDATIONS.md#result-algebra) on its exact subject, basis and\npredicate. All five core verdicts are available when evaluating an in-domain\nsubject. A request outside that domain returns `out_of_frame` at the invocation\nboundary; it is not forged into an in-domain judgment. Performance and effect state remain separate\ncoordinates. An omitted or unperformed evaluation is never a positive result.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/TRAVERSAL_OCCURRENCE_PROFILE.md#The%20%60a_c%60%20Traversal%20Occurrence%20Profile%20over%20Mutable%20Subjects%2FClosed%20Constraint%2C%20Judgment%2C%20Residual%2C%20And%20Stop%20Kinds",
          "start_line": 754
        }
      ],
      "key": "profile_result_coordinates",
      "statement": "Every admitted evaluation returns the shared result record; all five core verdicts remain available. Performance and effects are independent coordinates; omitted/unperformed evaluation is never positive. Domain decisions refine the shared algebra, not replace it: satisfied maps to the first positive decision in each judgment domain, invalid_basis only to invalid_basis, with original decision, predicate, evidence, residuals and stop retained. All judgments retain unchanged subject id/digest, evaluator, authority, evidence, provenance and decision; their kind determines applicable stops/residuals. valid/admitted/ready satisfy only their own predicates, never establish an intended external outcome. Missing decisive evidence with hold/gap/indeterminate remains indeterminate; demonstrated false predicates remain falsified with their mapped decision, including established-staleness hold. event_scope_compatible=false gives falsified compatibility with out_of_scope, not invocation-boundary out_of_frame.",
      "uncertainty": ""
    },
