      ],
      "key": "markov_candidate_and_promotion_gate",
      "statement": "Markov vocabulary is load-bearing but candidate-class. Source reports direction-level behavioral support, while conditional-independence test and multi-layer successor failed their predicate. Promotion requires direction-native conditional independence: given identity projection, remaining residual variation independent of target under plausible treatments. Gate cannot move to accommodate negative result. Claims presupposing established blanket remain revisable working commitments. Published overlays are candidate overlays of candidate construct, not certified blankets. Published entity cuts are lawful under their own test; unqualified entity candidates remain candidates. Status propagates downstream: tooling should default candidate-class publication and reserve formally-closed kind for real gate-backed cuts.",
