      "key": "world_model_evidence_preference",
      "statement": "Preferred evidence hierarchy: realized behavior and emitted records/events; available code/rules/configuration; interfaces/schemas; large-scale observational data; documents/catalogs/operator testimony. Code is high-fidelity when available, while realized behavior remains broader because proprietary or partial systems may be intelligible only through outputs/effects. This preference is not a mandatory code dependency.",
