      "conditions": ["Assess an exact semantic claim on declared subject/basis under its assurance rule."],
      "exceptions": ["Tolerated ambiguity remains explicit even with satisfaction."],
      "grounding": [
        {
          "end_line": 833,
          "quote": "An observed counterexample is `falsified`; missing decisive support is `indeterminate`.\nAn unusable basis is `invalid_basis`, and an out-of-domain request is\n`out_of_frame`. A proposed claim or an assessment not performed is never\n`satisfied` by default. `observed`, `derived`, `interpreted` and `composed`\ndescribe evidence provenance; they are not alternative success values.",
          "section_id": "repo://stdo-v3-generation-rc9/codex/5592168e26759f37e730aed12c030a6061709ec4/source/standards/WORLD_MODEL_METHOD.md#World%20Model%20Method%2FMethod%20Flow%2F4.%20Assure",
          "start_line": 829
        }
      ],
      "key": "assurance_predicate_results",
      "statement": "Qualify traced observations by binding purpose, interpreted predicate and actual observations under Assertions and observations. Predictive claims assess predictive adequacy: accuracy establishes no required construction outcome, and prediction error alone establishes no construction failure; distinct accounts/correction follow Bounded construction. Assurance should expose claim, observed/derived/interpreted/composed provenance, supporting surfaces, aspect-specific source authority and ambiguity/missingness. Shared return preserves original assurance outcome, evidence class and residual ambiguity on predicate 'claim C is supported on declared subject/basis under stated assurance rule'. Admissible support at required altitude satisfies; observed counterexample falsifies; missing decisive support is indeterminate; unusable basis invalid_basis; outside domain out_of_frame. Proposed/unperformed claims never satisfy by default; provenance labels are not success values.",
      "uncertainty": ""
