      "key": "entity_cut_representation",
      "statement": "Every published entity cut must be prompt-sufficient for reasoning. At minimum it should expose identity, boundary, authority, state, evidence, treatment, covariance and ambiguity. Effective blanket explicitness concerns the boundary where identity survives reinterpretation, not enumerated member columns. Boundary is interventional: survival across adjacent-domain treatment, not attribute membership. Schemas evidence identity rather than constitute it. In declared representation space, boundary takes low-rank geometric form; overlay should expose distributed evidence and identity-recovering projection. Otherwise discharge semantically.",
